---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '@data/site.json';

const updated = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
  month: 'long',
  day: 'numeric',
  year: 'numeric',
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Terms of use | ${site.name}`}
  description={`The terms that apply when you use ${site.name}.`}
  path="/terms/"
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { label: 'Terms of use', href: '/terms/' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="container page-top">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <div class="lead">
      <p>The short version: use the ideas, do not scrape the site.</p>
      <p>Last updated {updated}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container prose">
    <h2>What you can do</h2>
    <p>
      Browse, save ideas, copy a brief and show any of it to your tattoo artist.
      That is what the site is for.
    </p>

    <h2>What you cannot do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Scrape or bulk-download the images or the pages.</li>
      <li>Republish collections as your own.</li>
      <li>Use the content to train a model without written permission.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Images and copyright</h2>
    <p>
      Images belong to their creators or licensors. How they are sourced and
      credited is set out on the
      <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial standards</a> page. If you hold
      the rights to something published here and did not agree to it, write to
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and it comes down.
    </p>

    <h2>No professional guidance</h2>
    <p>
      Everything here is reference material for a conversation with a tattoo
      artist. Sizes, session times and prices are typical reports, not quotes.
      Nothing on this site is medical guidance. Questions about healing, skin
      reactions, allergies or removal belong with your artist or a doctor.
    </p>

    <h2>Adults</h2>
    <p>The site is written for adults and is not intended for anyone under 18.</p>

    <h2>Outbound links</h2>
    <p>
      We link to studios, artists and shops we do not control, and we are not
      responsible for what is on the other end.
    </p>

    <h2>Availability and accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      We try to keep page labels, dimensions and credits accurate, but reference
      material can contain errors. The site may change or become temporarily
      unavailable without notice. Verify dimensions, placement and feasibility
      with the artist who will draw and apply the tattoo.
    </p>

    <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
    <p>
      Send copyright, consent and factual correction requests to
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Include the page address,
      the specific image or text and enough information for us to review the
      request. Removing disputed material while it is checked does not confirm
      or deny ownership.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>These terms can change. The date at the top is when they last did.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
